42 years after her murder metro says  they now know who killed kim bryant the  department made that announcement today  in the cold case homicide joe mohler was  at the press conference he shows us how  they found out who did it  kim bryant was just 16 years old when  she was killed new dna testing links  johnny blake peterson to the crime  bryant a western high school student  went missing in 1979 she was kidnapped  raped and murdered her body was found in  the desert the case went cold but after  a donation to the department they were  able to send dna from her autopsy to a  lab in texas that lab linked dna found  on her body to the killer's family  members lieutenant ray spencer read a  statement from brian's father kim was a  beautiful girl with a bright future and  it makes me happy that something is  being done to help solve cases such as  hers police do not know if bryant and  peterson knew each other they did say  peterson briefly went to western high as  well peterson did have a criminal  background unfortunately there will be  no arrest or trial as peterson did die  back in 1993 reporting at metro  headquarters joe mohler live local now
 

